  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_intro",
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Introduction",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "> *AI authored to showcase ironpad capabilities.*\n\n# Spring-Mass-Damper System 🔧\n\nThe **spring-mass-damper** (SMD) is a fundamental mechanical model used in vibration analysis, control theory, and engineering design. A mass $m$ slides on a frictionless surface, coupled to a fixed wall by a spring with stiffness $k$ and a viscous damper with coefficient $c$.\n\n## Equation of Motion\n\nNewton's second law yields the linear ODE:\n\n$$m\\ddot{x} + c\\dot{x} + kx = F(t)$$\n\nwhere $x$ is displacement from equilibrium, $\\dot{x}$ velocity, $\\ddot{x}$ acceleration, and $F(t)$ an optional external force.\n\n## Key System Parameters\n\n- **Natural frequency**: $\\omega_n = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{k}{m}}$, the oscillation rate of the undamped system\n- **Damping ratio**: $\\zeta = \\dfrac{c}{2\\sqrt{mk}}$, a dimensionless measure of dissipation\n\n## Damping Regimes\n\n| Regime | Condition | Response |\n|--------|-----------|----------|\n| **Underdamped** | $\\zeta < 1$ | Decaying oscillation, bounces before settling |\n| **Critically damped** | $\\zeta = 1$ | Fastest return with no overshoot |\n| **Overdamped** | $\\zeta > 1$ | Sluggish exponential decay, no oscillation |\n\n## External Forcing\n\nEnable **External Forcing** to apply $F(t) = A\\sin(\\omega_f t)$. When the driving frequency $\\omega_f$ approaches $\\omega_n$, **resonance** amplifies the response, especially for low damping.\n\nAdjust the sliders to move between regimes and watch the physical diagram, waveform, and dashboard update live.",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_controls",
      "order": 1,
      "label": "Controls",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "(\n    ui::slider(\"mass\", 0.5, 10.0)\n        .step(0.1)\n        .label(\"Mass m (kg)\")\n        .default_value(2.0),\n    ui::slider(\"k\", 1.0, 100.0)\n        .step(0.5)\n        .label(\"Spring k (N/m)\")\n        .default_value(20.0),\n    ui::slider(\"c\", 0.0, 30.0)\n        .step(0.1)\n        .label(\"Damping c (Ns/m)\")\n        .default_value(2.0),\n    ui::slider(\"force_amp\", 0.0, 50.0)\n        .step(0.5)\n        .label(\"Force Amplitude (N)\")\n        .default_value(10.0),\n    ui::slider(\"force_freq\", 0.1, 10.0)\n        .step(0.1)\n        .label(\"Force Frequency (Hz)\")\n        .default_value(1.0),\n    ui::checkbox(\"forcing_on\")\n        .label(\"External Forcing\")\n        .default_value(false),\n)",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "collapsed": true,
      "saved_output": "[{\"Interactive\":{\"kind\":\"slider\",\"config\":\"{\\\"default\\\":2.0,\\\"label\\\":\\\"Mass m (kg)\\\",\\\"max\\\":10.0,\\\"min\\\":0.5,\\\"name\\\":\\\"mass\\\",\\\"step\\\":0.1}\"}},{\"Interactive\":{\"kind\":\"slider\",\"config\":\"{\\\"default\\\":20.0,\\\"label\\\":\\\"Spring k (N/m)\\\",\\\"max\\\":100.0,\\\"min\\\":1.0,\\\"name\\\":\\\"k\\\",\\\"step\\\":0.5}\"}},{\"Interactive\":{\"kind\":\"slider\",\"config\":\"{\\\"default\\\":2.0,\\\"label\\\":\\\"Damping c (Ns/m)\\\",\\\"max\\\":30.0,\\\"min\\\":0.0,\\\"name\\\":\\\"c\\\",\\\"step\\\":0.1}\"}},{\"Interactive\":{\"kind\":\"slider\",\"config\":\"{\\\"default\\\":10.0,\\\"label\\\":\\\"Force Amplitude (N)\\\",\\\"max\\\":50.0,\\\"min\\\":0.0,\\\"name\\\":\\\"force_amp\\\",\\\"step\\\":0.5}\"}},{\"Interactive\":{\"kind\":\"slider\",\"config\":\"{\\\"default\\\":1.0,\\\"label\\\":\\\"Force Frequency (Hz)\\\",\\\"max\\\":10.0,\\\"min\\\":0.1,\\\"name\\\":\\\"force_freq\\\",\\\"step\\\":0.1}\"}},{\"Interactive\":{\"kind\":\"checkbox\",\"config\":\"{\\\"default\\\":false,\\\"label\\\":\\\"External Forcing\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"forcing_on\\\"}\"}}]"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_sim",
      "order": 2,
      "label": "Spring-Mass-Damper Simulation",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "// Spring-Mass-Damper live simulation.\n//\n// Top region:  physical diagram — wall, spring (zigzag), damper (dashpot), mass block.\n// Bottom region: rolling displacement-vs-time waveform.\n// Telemetry is published each tick for the Dashboard cell to consume.\n\nconst PI: f64 = std::f64::consts::PI;\n\nconst W: u32 = 800;\nconst H: u32 = 400;\nconst DT: f64 = 1.0 / 30.0;\nconst SUB_STEPS: u32 = 20;\nconst MAX_HIST: usize = 600;\n\n// Canvas layout\nconst TOP_H: u32 = 250;\nconst BOT_Y: u32 = 256;\n\n// Physical geometry (pixels)\nconst WALL_X: f64 = 90.0;\nconst EQ_X: f64 = 380.0;    // equilibrium left edge of mass block\nconst SPRING_Y: f64 = 105.0; // y of spring centerline\nconst DAMPER_Y: f64 = 148.0; // y of damper centerline\nconst MASS_W: f64 = 55.0;\nconst MASS_H: f64 = 80.0;\nconst MASS_CY: f64 = 127.0;  // vertical center of mass block\nconst DISP_SCALE: f64 = 40.0; // pixels per metre\n\nstruct SpringMassDamper {\n    x: f64,\n    v: f64,\n    time: f64,\n    history: Vec<f64>,\n}\n\n// ── Drawing helpers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nfn safe_set(canvas: &mut Canvas, x: i32, y: i32, c: (u8, u8, u8)) {\n    if x >= 0 && y >= 0 && (x as u32) < W && (y as u32) < H {\n        canvas.set_pixel(x as u32, y as u32, c);\n    }\n}\n\nfn draw_line(canvas: &mut Canvas, x0: i32, y0: i32, x1: i32, y1: i32, c: (u8, u8, u8)) {\n    let dx = (x1 - x0).abs();\n    let dy = -(y1 - y0).abs();\n    let sx = if x0 < x1 { 1i32 } else { -1i32 };\n    let sy = if y0 < y1 { 1i32 } else { -1i32 };\n    let mut err = dx + dy;\n    let (mut px, mut py) = (x0, y0);\n    loop {\n        safe_set(canvas, px, py, c);\n        if px == x1 && py == y1 { break; }\n        let e2 = 2 * err;\n        if e2 >= dy { err += dy; px += sx; }\n        if e2 <= dx { err += dx; py += sy; }\n    }\n}\n\nfn draw_thick_line(canvas: &mut Canvas, x0: i32, y0: i32, x1: i32, y1: i32, t: i32, c: (u8, u8, u8)) {\n    for oy in -t..=t {\n        for ox in -t..=t {\n            if ox * ox + oy * oy <= t * t {\n                draw_line(canvas, x0 + ox, y0 + oy, x1 + ox, y1 + oy, c);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfn fill_rect(canvas: &mut Canvas, x: i32, y: i32, w: i32, h: i32, c: (u8, u8, u8)) {\n    for dy in 0..h {\n        for dx in 0..w {\n            safe_set(canvas, x + dx, y + dy, c);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Draw a coiled spring as a sine-wave zigzag between (x0, yc) and (x1, yc).\nfn draw_spring(\n    canvas: &mut Canvas,\n    x0: f64, x1: f64, yc: f64,\n    n_coils: usize, amp: f64,\n    c: (u8, u8, u8),\n) {\n    let lead = 12.0;\n    if x1 < x0 + 2.0 * lead + 4.0 { return; }\n    let span = x1 - x0 - 2.0 * lead;\n    let steps = n_coils * 12;\n\n    // Horizontal lead-in from wall to start of coils\n    draw_line(canvas, x0 as i32, yc as i32, (x0 + lead) as i32, yc as i32, c);\n\n    let mut prev = (x0 + lead, yc);\n    for i in 1..=steps {\n        let t = i as f64 / steps as f64;\n        let sx = x0 + lead + t * span;\n        let sy = yc - amp * (t * n_coils as f64 * 2.0 * PI).sin();\n        draw_line(canvas, prev.0 as i32, prev.1 as i32, sx as i32, sy as i32, c);\n        prev = (sx, sy);\n    }\n\n    // Horizontal lead-out from end of coils to mass\n    draw_line(canvas, (x1 - lead) as i32, yc as i32, x1 as i32, yc as i32, c);\n}\n\n/// Draw a dashpot damper between (x0, yc) and (x1, yc).\nfn draw_damper(\n    canvas: &mut Canvas,\n    x0: f64, x1: f64, yc: f64,\n    c: (u8, u8, u8),\n) {\n    let lead = 12.0;\n    let box_len = 44.0;\n    let box_h = 11.0;\n    let bx0 = x0 + lead;\n    let bx1 = bx0 + box_len;\n\n    // Lead-in from wall to cylinder\n    draw_line(canvas, x0 as i32, yc as i32, bx0 as i32, yc as i32, c);\n\n    // Cylinder: top wall, bottom wall, left cap\n    draw_line(canvas, bx0 as i32, (yc - box_h) as i32, bx1 as i32, (yc - box_h) as i32, c);\n    draw_line(canvas, bx0 as i32, (yc + box_h) as i32, bx1 as i32, (yc + box_h) as i32, c);\n    draw_line(canvas, bx0 as i32, (yc - box_h) as i32, bx0 as i32, (yc + box_h) as i32, c);\n\n    // Piston plate inside cylinder\n    let piston_x = bx0 + 0.38 * box_len;\n    draw_line(canvas, piston_x as i32, (yc - box_h + 2.0) as i32, piston_x as i32, (yc + box_h - 2.0) as i32, c);\n\n    // Piston rod from plate to mass\n    draw_line(canvas, piston_x as i32, yc as i32, x1 as i32, yc as i32, c);\n\n    // End cap at mass side\n    draw_line(canvas, x1 as i32, (yc - box_h) as i32, x1 as i32, (yc + box_h) as i32, c);\n}\n\n// ── Simulation trait ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimpl Simulation for SpringMassDamper {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        Self { x: 1.0, v: 0.0, time: 0.0, history: Vec::new() }\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> Canvas {\n        let m          = sim::read::<f64>(\"mass\").unwrap_or(2.0);\n        let k          = sim::read::<f64>(\"k\").unwrap_or(20.0);\n        let c_damp     = sim::read::<f64>(\"c\").unwrap_or(2.0);\n        let force_amp  = sim::read::<f64>(\"force_amp\").unwrap_or(10.0);\n        let force_freq = sim::read::<f64>(\"force_freq\").unwrap_or(1.0);\n        let forcing    = sim::read::<f64>(\"forcing_on\").unwrap_or(0.0) > 0.5;\n\n        // Sub-stepped forward-Euler integration for stability\n        let sub_dt = DT / SUB_STEPS as f64;\n        for _ in 0..SUB_STEPS {\n            let f_ext = if forcing {\n                force_amp * (2.0 * PI * force_freq * self.time).sin()\n            } else {\n                0.0\n            };\n            let a = (f_ext - c_damp * self.v - k * self.x) / m;\n            self.v += a * sub_dt;\n            self.x += self.v * sub_dt;\n            self.time += sub_dt;\n        }\n\n        self.x = self.x.clamp(-5.0, 5.0);\n        self.v = self.v.clamp(-50.0, 50.0);\n\n        self.history.push(self.x);\n        if self.history.len() > MAX_HIST {\n            self.history.remove(0);\n        }\n\n        // Publish telemetry for the dashboard\n        let ke      = 0.5 * m * self.v * self.v;\n        let pe      = 0.5 * k * self.x * self.x;\n        let zeta    = c_damp / (2.0 * (m * k).sqrt());\n        let omega_n = (k / m).sqrt();\n        sim::emit(\"displacement\", &self.x);\n        sim::emit(\"velocity\",     &self.v);\n        sim::emit(\"ke\",           &ke);\n        sim::emit(\"pe\",           &pe);\n        sim::emit(\"zeta\",         &zeta);\n        sim::emit(\"omega_n\",      &omega_n);\n\n        // ── Render ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n        let mut canvas = Canvas::new(W, H);\n        canvas.fill((15, 15, 25));\n\n        let mass_left = (EQ_X + self.x * DISP_SCALE)\n            .clamp(WALL_X + 28.0, W as f64 - MASS_W - 10.0);\n\n        // ── Wall ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n        let wall_c = (70, 70, 90);\n        fill_rect(&mut canvas, (WALL_X - 10.0) as i32, 50, 10, 160, wall_c);\n        let mut hy = 58i32;\n        while hy < 205 {\n            draw_line(\n                &mut canvas,\n                (WALL_X - 10.0) as i32, hy,\n                (WALL_X - 18.0) as i32, hy - 8,\n                wall_c,\n            );\n            hy += 12;\n        }\n\n        // ── Spring ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n        draw_spring(&mut canvas, WALL_X, mass_left, SPRING_Y, 8, 10.0, (60, 190, 255));\n\n        // ── Damper ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n        draw_damper(&mut canvas, WALL_X, mass_left, DAMPER_Y, (255, 165, 50));\n\n        // ── Mass block ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n        let mtop = (MASS_CY - MASS_H / 2.0) as i32;\n        let mbot = (MASS_CY + MASS_H / 2.0) as i32;\n        fill_rect(\n            &mut canvas,\n            mass_left as i32, mtop,\n            MASS_W as i32, MASS_H as i32,\n            (35, 150, 95),\n        );\n        let out_c = (90, 230, 155);\n        let ml = mass_left as i32;\n        let mr = (mass_left + MASS_W) as i32;\n        draw_thick_line(&mut canvas, ml, mtop, mr, mtop, 1, out_c);\n        draw_thick_line(&mut canvas, ml, mbot, mr, mbot, 1, out_c);\n        draw_thick_line(&mut canvas, ml, mtop, ml, mbot, 1, out_c);\n        draw_thick_line(&mut canvas, mr, mtop, mr, mbot, 1, out_c);\n\n        // ── External force arrow ─────────────────────────────────────────\n        if forcing {\n            let f_now = force_amp * (2.0 * PI * force_freq * self.time).sin();\n            let arrow_px = (f_now * 3.0).clamp(-90.0, 90.0) as i32;\n            let ay = MASS_CY as i32;\n            let (ax0, ax1) = if arrow_px >= 0 {\n                (mr + 5, mr + 5 + arrow_px)\n            } else {\n                (ml - 5, ml - 5 + arrow_px)\n            };\n            draw_thick_line(&mut canvas, ax0, ay, ax1, ay, 2, (255, 70, 70));\n            // Arrowhead\n            if ax1 != ax0 {\n                let tip = ax1;\n                let dir = if ax1 > ax0 { 1 } else { -1 };\n                for k in 1..=5 {\n                    draw_line(&mut canvas, tip, ay, tip - dir * k, ay - k, (255, 70, 70));\n                    draw_line(&mut canvas, tip, ay, tip - dir * k, ay + k, (255, 70, 70));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Equilibrium dashed line\n        let eq_px = (EQ_X + MASS_W / 2.0) as i32;\n        let mut ey = 50i32;\n        while ey < TOP_H as i32 {\n            safe_set(&mut canvas, eq_px, ey, (50, 50, 72));\n            ey += 5;\n        }\n\n        // ── Waveform region ───────────────────────────────────────────────\n        // Separator line\n        for px in 0..W {\n            safe_set(&mut canvas, px as i32, BOT_Y as i32, (40, 40, 60));\n        }\n\n        let wave_cy = BOT_Y as f64 + (H - BOT_Y) as f64 * 0.5;\n        let wave_amp_px = (H - BOT_Y) as f64 * 0.42;\n\n        // Zero line\n        for px in 0..W {\n            safe_set(&mut canvas, px as i32, wave_cy as i32, (40, 40, 60));\n        }\n\n        if self.history.len() > 1 {\n            let n = self.history.len();\n            let x_scale = W as f64 / MAX_HIST as f64;\n            for i in 1..n {\n                let px0 = ((i - 1) as f64 * x_scale) as i32;\n                let px1 = (i as f64 * x_scale) as i32;\n                let py0 = (wave_cy - self.history[i - 1] / 5.0 * wave_amp_px) as i32;\n                let py1 = (wave_cy - self.history[i]     / 5.0 * wave_amp_px) as i32;\n                let bright = (70 + i * 185 / n) as u8;\n                draw_line(&mut canvas, px0, py0, px1, py1, (0, bright / 2, bright));\n            }\n        }\n\n        canvas\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 {\n        30\n    }\n}",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "collapsed": true,
      "saved_output": "[{\"Text\":\"(output too large to embed; run the cell to regenerate it)\"}]"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_dashboard",
      "order": 3,
      "label": "Dashboard",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "struct Dashboard {\n    tick: u32,\n}\n\nimpl LiveView for Dashboard {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        Self { tick: 0 }\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> LiveContent {\n        self.tick += 1;\n\n        let x       = sim::read::<f64>(\"displacement\").unwrap_or(0.0);\n        let v       = sim::read::<f64>(\"velocity\").unwrap_or(0.0);\n        let ke      = sim::read::<f64>(\"ke\").unwrap_or(0.0);\n        let pe      = sim::read::<f64>(\"pe\").unwrap_or(0.0);\n        let total   = ke + pe;\n        let zeta    = sim::read::<f64>(\"zeta\").unwrap_or(0.0);\n        let omega_n = sim::read::<f64>(\"omega_n\").unwrap_or(0.0);\n\n        let (regime, regime_color) = if zeta < 0.99 {\n            (\"UNDERDAMPED\", \"#4fc3f7\")\n        } else if zeta < 1.01 {\n            (\"CRITICALLY DAMPED\", \"#ffd700\")\n        } else {\n            (\"OVERDAMPED\", \"#ff6b6b\")\n        };\n\n        LiveContent::Html(format!(\n            r#\"<div style=\"font-family: monospace; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0a0a1a, #1a1a2e); color: #e0e0e0; padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #2a2a3a;\">\n  <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap;\">\n    <div style=\"background: #1a1a2e; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid #2a2a3a; min-width: 140px;\">\n      <div style=\"color: #888; font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; margin-bottom: 6px;\">STATE</div>\n      <div>x = <span style=\"color: #4fc3f7;\">{x:.4}</span> m</div>\n      <div>v = <span style=\"color: #ff6b6b;\">{v:.4}</span> m/s</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"background: #1a1a2e; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid #2a2a3a; min-width: 160px;\">\n      <div style=\"color: #888; font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; margin-bottom: 6px;\">ENERGY</div>\n      <div>KE = <span style=\"color: #ff6b6b;\">{ke:.3}</span> J</div>\n      <div>PE = <span style=\"color: #4fc3f7;\">{pe:.3}</span> J</div>\n      <div>Total = <span style=\"color: #44cc44;\">{total:.3}</span> J</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"background: #1a1a2e; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid #2a2a3a; min-width: 160px;\">\n      <div style=\"color: #888; font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; margin-bottom: 6px;\">SYSTEM</div>\n      <div>&zeta; = {zeta:.3}</div>\n      <div>&omega;&#x2099; = {omega_n:.2} rad/s</div>\n      <div style=\"color: {regime_color}; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 4px;\">{regime}</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.7em; color: #555; text-align: right;\">tick #{tick}</div>\n</div>\"#,\n            tick = self.tick,\n        ))\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 {\n        10\n    }\n}",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "collapsed": true,
      "saved_output": "[{\"LiveView\":{\"fps\":10,\"kind\":\"html\",\"content\":\"<div style=\\\"font-family: monospace; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0a0a1a, #1a1a2e); color: #e0e0e0; padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #2a2a3a;\\\">\\n  <div style=\\\"display: flex; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap;\\\">\\n    <div style=\\\"background: #1a1a2e; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid #2a2a3a; min-width: 140px;\\\">\\n      <div style=\\\"color: #888; font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; margin-bottom: 6px;\\\">STATE</div>\\n      <div>x = <span style=\\\"color: #4fc3f7;\\\">0.2973</span> m</div>\\n      <div>v = <span style=\\\"color: #ff6b6b;\\\">-2.5188</span> m/s</div>\\n    </div>\\n    <div style=\\\"background: #1a1a2e; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid #2a2a3a; min-width: 160px;\\\">\\n      <div style=\\\"color: #888; font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; margin-bottom: 6px;\\\">ENERGY</div>\\n      <div>KE = <span style=\\\"color: #ff6b6b;\\\">6.344</span> J</div>\\n      <div>PE = <span style=\\\"color: #4fc3f7;\\\">0.884</span> J</div>\\n      <div>Total = <span style=\\\"color: #44cc44;\\\">7.228</span> J</div>\\n    </div>\\n    <div style=\\\"background: #1a1a2e; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid #2a2a3a; min-width: 160px;\\\">\\n      <div style=\\\"color: #888; font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; margin-bottom: 6px;\\\">SYSTEM</div>\\n      <div>&zeta; = 0.158</div>\\n      <div>&omega;&#x2099; = 3.16 rad/s</div>\\n      <div style=\\\"color: #4fc3f7; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 4px;\\\">UNDERDAMPED</div>\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n  <div style=\\\"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.7em; color: #555; text-align: right;\\\">tick #1</div>\\n</div>\"}}]"
    }
  ]
}
